  "description": "Fan out a converged devague plan's dependency waves to parallel agents in isolated git worktrees, one agent per task per wave, with TDD-gated merges by the main agent. Human gates: the exported spec, the implementation split plan (task map + per-task agent/model proposal + go/no-go), and the final PR. The devague CLI stays deterministic and non-orchestrating (#20) — it only *describes* the graph via `devague plan waves`; the operator (main agent) performs the fan-out. Use when the user says \"assign to workforce\", \"fan out the plan\", \"parallel subagents\", or after /spec-to-plan exports a plan. Authored and maintained in agentculture/devague (origin = devague); steward pulls this skill from here and broadcasts it to the AgentCulture mesh — it is NOT vendored from steward like the other skills here.",
